  "notes": "General option, University Park (of two options — the other, Hydrogeology, swaps in a different elective structure). Major code 'GEOSCI' avoids colliding with the GEOSC department prefix used across many other Earth and Mineral Sciences majors. The bulletin's real-world plan places GEOSC 472B (Field Geology II) in a required summer term between Third and Fourth Year — this planner only models summer as an optional student choice, not a mandatory plan term, so GEOSC 472B is scheduled in a regular fall/spring term instead. 'Advanced GEOSC elective' and 'Supporting course' pools are modeled generically, same convention as BIOL's 400-level elective groups. Real prereq-fix fallout: CHEM 110 now requires MATH 22, which itself requires MATH 21, MATH 4, and MATH 3 in turn -- a full remedial placement chain never otherwise scheduled in this plan -- added all four as explicit early-semester items. The engine's own scheduler pushes CHEM 110 (and its downstream 111/112/113) out to whichever later term MATH 22 actually completes in; the whole plan still finishes in 8 terms at this major's existing 17cr/semester cap.",
